{%- comment -%}
  Real flag image, not emoji. Unicode flag emoji (regional-indicator
  letter pairs) render as literal two-letter text on Windows and many
  Android builds -- those platforms ship no glyph for them at all -- which
  is what made the currency picker look broken/buggy there. An <img>
  renders identically on every platform. flagcdn.com also covers every
  ISO country code, not just a hand-picked list, which matters now that
  an EU market (27 countries) is in the mix.

  Only use this where real markup can render -- the trigger button, a
  closed select's icon. Never inside a native <option>, which can only
  hold plain text; there, skip the flag and just use clear text instead.
  Usage: {% render 'country-flag', iso_code: country.iso_code %}
{%- endcomment -%}
<img
  src="https://flagcdn.com/{{ iso_code | downcase }}.svg"
  alt=""
  width="20"
  height="15"
  loading="lazy"
  class="country-flag-icon"
>
